ct as a Senior Android Developer (5+ years experience).\nI have an existing Android app built with Jetpack Compose (Kotlin).\nI want to implement a reliable Adhan (Azan) alarm system for Bangladesh prayer times.\n\nRequirements:\n\nUse AlarmManager (setExactAndAllowWhileIdle) — do NOT use WorkManager for prayer alarms.\n\nCalculate accurate Bangladesh prayer times (Fajr, Dhuhr, Asr, Maghrib, Isha) using a proper Islamic calculation method (Karachi method, Hanafi madhab).\n\nAt each prayer time (e.g., Fajr 5:30 AM), the app must:\n\nPlay full Adhan audio\n\nShow a foreground notification\n\nWork even when the app is killed, in Doze mode, or phone is locked\n\nImplement using:\n\nAlarmManager\n\nBroadcastReceiver\n\nForegroundService (mandatory for audio playback)\n\nHandle Android 12+ exact alarm permission, battery optimization, and background restrictions correctly.\n\nUse USAGE_ALARM audio attributes so Adhan is audible even in silent/low priority states.\n\nStructure the solution cleanly:\n\nPrayerTimeCalculator\n\nAdhanScheduler\n\nAdhanReceiver\n\nAdhanForegroundService\n\nAssume the project already exists — explain where each component should be placed.\n\nFollow best practices, clean architecture, and production-ready code.\n\nProvide minimal but complete Kotlin code snippets, not pseudo-code.\n\nOutput expectation:\n\nClear explanation of architecture\n\nExact implementation steps\n\nKotlin code for each component\n\nAndroidManifest permissions \u0026 declarations\n\nCommon pitfalls why Adhan doesn’t play and how this approach fixes them\n\nThink like you are building a real Islamic prayer app for Bangladesh users. Accuracy and reliability are critical.\n\u003c/user_query\u003e&quot;}]},{&quot;role&quot;:&quot;assistant&quot;,&quot;content&quot;:[{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;text&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;I\u0027ll help you implement a reliable Adhan alarm system for Bangladesh prayer times. Let me first explore your existing project structure to understand th